<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">South Pacific Nuclear Free Zone Treaty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1985">1985</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Treaty of Rarotonga</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The South Pacific Nuclear Free Zone Treaty, or Treaty of Rarotonga, was signed at Rarotonga in the Cook Islands on 6 August 1985 by members of the South Pacific Forum, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>. It bans the manufacture, possession, stationing and testing of nuclear explosive devices in the zone and the dumping of radioactive waste at sea. It entered into force in 1986.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/south-pacific-nuclear-free-zone-treaty.jpg" alt="South Pacific Nuclear Free Zone Treaty" width="320" height="163" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original uploader: JWB · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nwfz.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
